# Repo-level semgrep ignore list.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (do not delete it):
# semgrep's BUILT-IN default ignore list contains `test/` and `tests/`.
# With no `.semgrepignore` at the repo root, every `packages/*/tests/**`
# path was filtered out *before* the rules ran, so CC040 and CC041 —
# the two rules scoped exclusively to test paths via
# `paths.include: ["**/tests/**"]` — scanned ZERO targets and enforced
# nothing while ten real CC041 violations accumulated behind them
# (`make lint-claude`, Makefile `lint-claude` target).
#
# Semgrep REPLACES its whole default list with this file, so everything
# that should stay ignored is enumerated below. Test paths are
# deliberately absent — that is the entire point of the file. Patterns
# use .gitignore syntax and match at any depth.
#
# The regression backstop lives in
# packages/core/tests/unit/scripts/test_semgrep_rule_selftests.py
# (`test_ci_shape_scan_reaches_test_paths`): it runs semgrep the way
# `make lint-claude` does — a DIRECTORY target, not explicit file paths —
# and fails if `Targets scanned` ever drops back to 0.

# --- Version control + tooling caches -------------------------------------
.git/
.hg/
.svn/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
__pycache__/

# --- Python environments --------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env/
*.egg-info/

# --- Node / frontend ------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.npm/
.yarn/
*.min.js
*.min.css

# --- Build + generated output ---------------------------------------------
build/
dist/
vendor/
generated/
.docusaurus/
coverage_html/
htmlcov/
test-reports/

# --- semgrep's own scratch space ------------------------------------------
.semgrep/
.semgrep_logs/
